    "tools": "Wide kadhai with lid, small steel cup, tongs, gas",
    "serves": 2,
    "cover": "cover",
    "ingredients": [
      {
        "q": "~2 cups (about 450 ml)",
        "n": "Idli batter (ready or homemade)",
        "tag": "idli-batter",
        "img": "i-batter",
        "alt": [
          "dosa-batter"
        ]
      },
      {
        "q": "~2 tbsp",
        "n": "Oil",
        "tag": "oil",
        "img": "i-oil"
      },
      {
        "q": "~2 tsp",
        "n": "Cumin seeds (jeera)",
        "tag": "cumin",
        "img": "i-cumin"
      },
      {
        "q": "~1/2 cup, for the steel cup",
        "n": "Water",
        "tag": "water",
        "img": "i-water"
      },
      {
        "q": "to serve",
        "n": "Chutney or pickle (tamarind pachadi, coconut chutney)",
        "tag": "chutney",
        "img": "i-chutney",
        "opt": true,
        "alt": [
          "tamarind-chutney"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "t": "Pour about 2 tbsp oil into a wide kadhai and heat it on the gas.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-oil-1",
          "s-oil-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Add about 2 tsp cumin seeds and let them sizzle in the oil.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-cumin-1",
          "s-cumin-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Pour in about 2 cups idli batter so it covers the whole base.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-batter-1",
          "s-batter-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Fill a small steel cup with water and press it into the middle of the batter.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-cup-1",
          "s-cup-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Put a lid on the kadhai and let it cook.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-lid-1",
          "s-lid-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Cook until the top looks fluffy and dry. The water in the cup bubbles and steams the top.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-cook-1",
          "s-cook-2",
          "s-cook-3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Lift the steel cup out with tongs.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-remove-1",
          "s-remove-2",
          "s-remove-3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Loosen the edges all around.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-loosen-1",
          "s-loosen-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Flip the donut onto a plate, crispy cumin side up.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-flip-1",
          "s-flip-2",
          "s-flip-3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Cut it into triangle slices.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-cut-1",
          "s-cut-2",
          "s-cut-3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Serve hot with chutney or pickle.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-serve-1",
          "s-serve-2",
          "s-serve-3"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "tags": [
      "gas",
      "one-pot"
    ],
    "notes": "No amounts, heat level or cooking time are given in the video, so all amounts (~) and the 20 min total are my estimates. The base turns crisp and golden and carries the cumin; the 'toasted jeera on top' is just that side after the flip. Idli batter may be replaced by thick dosa batter (alt tag). The video showed the creator's own sides (chintapandu pachadi, idli, poha) but no name or handle on screen."
